content.text:
There it is. Before commit `5fddc49c`, the `outputHookResponse` function was setting `SystemMessage`:

```go
// Before:
resp := hookResponse{
    SystemMessage: reason,  // ← This showed the message to the user
}

// After:
resp := hookResponse{
    HookSpecificOutput: &hookSpecificOutput{
        HookEventName:     "SessionStart",
        AdditionalContext: context,  // ← This only goes into agent context
    },
}
```

The format fix moved the "Powered by Entire" text from `systemMessage` (user-visible) to `additionalContext` (agent-only). The message still reaches me, but it's no longer displayed in your terminal.

The fix is to include both — set `systemMessage` so you see it, and keep `additionalContext` so the agent gets it too.

